Spec: Activity type

Purpose:
  The rolling and sliding activities a ride can have and their stored ids.

Owns:
  ./activity_type.dart
  /test/domain/activity_type_test.dart

References:
  /docs/specs/history/04-domain.md

Must:
  The types are longboard, skateboard, mountainboard, rollerblades, rollerskates, scooter, snowboard,
    ski and other; declaration order is the order of every picker. Skate types come first, snow
    types after them, `other` last.
  Each type has a stable uppercase id stored in `Ride.typ`, such as `LONGBOARD`, `SNOWBOARD` and `SKI`.
    Ids are never renamed: rides already stored keep resolving to their type.
  @ActivityType.isSnow is true for snowboard and ski only (#97).
  @ActivityType.fromId returns `null` for an unknown or missing id.
  @ActivityType.defaultType is longboard.

Must not:
  Hold labels or icons; those are UI concerns.

Example:
  `@ActivityType.fromId('LONGBOARD')`: longboard
  `@ActivityType.fromId('SNOWBOARD')`: snowboard
  `@ActivityType.fromId('SURF')`: `null`
